# Omniscience: "You may cast spells from your hand without paying their mana costs" (CR 118.9). Bot1 puts it onto the
# battlefield with Show and Tell on turn 1 and keeps {U}{B} floating (Mox Jet's black, the Island's blue). Walking Ballista
# cast without paying its mana cost has X 0, the only legal choice (CR 107.3b): no X is announced, though the {U}{B} in the
# pool could have paid X = 1 if the line's "X: 1" had been asked for, so it enters with no counters and dies (CR 704.5f),
# and the pool is untouched. Bonecrusher Giant's Adventure, Stomp, is cast the same way, as that face (CR 715.3a), for nothing:
# 2 damage to Bot2, and the card goes on its adventure. The pool still holds {U}{B} at the end: nothing was paid for either.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Omniscience
Walking Ballista
Bonecrusher Giant
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Lightning Bolt x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Omniscience)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {U}{B}
Bot1.Hand.Walking Ballista.Cast(X: 1; Ability: Without paying)
? Bot1.Mana = {U}{B}
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Walking Ballista; Show and Tell; Black Lotus
Bot1.Hand.Bonecrusher Giant.Cast(Bot2; Ability: Stomp: Without paying)
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Mana = {U}{B}

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Mox Jet; Omniscience
Bot1.Graveyard = Walking Ballista; Show and Tell; Black Lotus
Bot1.Hand.Count = 0
Exile = Bonecrusher Giant
Bot2.Life = 18
